            <p>American cruising has blossomed into a distinct way to see and experience rivers, coastlines and small port towns throughout the United States. When travellers think about cruises, typically they envision huge ocean liners that cross international waters, but there is a more intimate and quieter form of cruising, looking inward at American heritage scenery and culture. That's where American cruise lines have carved out a speciality for themselves, offering cruises that focus on regional history and personalised service. </p>

            <p>I think that people who select American programs are looking for something more substantial than mass entertainment. The vibe is usually low-key, educational, and scenic, with opportunities for passengers to disembark in ports on rivers like the Mississippi or along the coastlines of New England and Alaska. The focus is more on comfort, connection and artistry than crowds and spectacle. </p>

            <h2>American Cruise Lines Getting Back to Domestic Discovery</h2>

            <p>American cruise lines focus on travel along American waterways. Instead of traversing oceans to far-off continents, these cruises focus on national parks, historic towns and cultural attractions that embody the country's history. Ships have a smaller size, which still fits in some ports that larger ships can't. </p>

            <p>Passengers generally immerse themselves in the onboard experience through regional cuisine, guest lecturers and enrichment programs that tie them to each destination. Visitors have the opportunity to take in panoramic views from large lounges and open decks, picking up an appreciation of local customs, architecture and nature. It's an approach for travellers looking for the road less travelled rather than a comatose tour. </p>

            <h2>Pride of America: The Only US-Flagged Cruise Ship Sailing Hawaii</h2>

            <p>Pride of america The ship Pride of the U.S.A is a name that always comes to mind when we talk about America-centric cruising. Operated by Norwegian Cruise Line, this ship sails the Hawaiian Islands under a United States flag. It provides visitors with a chance to visit several Hawaiian islands without the need for international travel. </p>

            <p>What's most conspicuous about Pride of America is that it features domestic cruising and resort-style cruising combined into one. Passengers can wake up to a new island each morning, relishing volcanic landscapes, beaches and cultural heritage without having to repack between ports. This is a new trend within the world of cruising convenience and American-based, hassle-free travel. </p>

